      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had forgotten what fcm_exclude did (though I did check automotive isn\u0027t in that list).\n\nhal_implementation_test\u0027s job is to check to see if a HAL is implemented on cuttlefish. This is a cuttlefish specific test (and a device test - verifying these XML files shouldn\u0027t require a device) which we use as a general proxy for our testing coverage/health/ability to maintain HALs.\n\nSo, in this case, I think we should have a separate host test verifying that entries in the compatibility matrix don\u0027t have typos (I know there was a bug for this long ago, but we didn\u0027t have the data easily available for it then).",
      "parentUuid": "b1bec6fd_0310c6cf",
